From 12948c50a7d143794b1afd963710ba88f53a5052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:57:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(picker): remove redundant singleton reads and home path
 allocation [daveey]

Profile representative model.options fixture: singleton dispatch parsed auth.json even for seeders that never consumed it (126 total reads -> 74). Load only in the consuming branches. Reuse bounded immutable expanded Path syntax, with live env expansion each call, and avoid Path reconstruction on warm home-key hits. No new credential/config/provider cache and no changes to plugin due checks.

RED/GREEN: singleton dispatch 4 expected failures/2 passes ->6 passes; immutable Path identity 1 expected failure/3 passes ->4 passes; warm home-key allocation refusal fails ->passes. Regression:118 files,987 pass,4 preexisting skips, retries disabled. Ten unchanged replay tests pass; all50 measured shared samples57.40-100.54ms (worst0.27647% core at11/400 calls/s), original best-of-five0.158-0.177%, unchanged0.3% budget. An earlier intermediate sample110.65ms (0.3043%) is retained as a failure, not acceptance. scripts/check --base origin/main passes. J owns full RPC/P1/C18 acceptance.
